A command whose shifted sits under a line directive naming another file of the
module. Its unused parameter is found by the one configuration that compiled
main.go, so it is reported, at the position the directive gives it, as plain's is.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27
-- deadset.json --
{"target": {"kind": "application"}}
-- main.go --
package main

func main() { println(plain(1), shifted(2)) }

func plain(unused int) int {
	return 0
}

//line shadow.txt:3:1
func shifted(also int) int {
	return 0
}
-- shadow.txt --
a generated listing the directive above points into, long enough to render
every column the shifted declaration's lines use once remapped onto it here
func shifted(also int) int { and the rest of the third line of this listing }
	return 0, which is the second line of the remapped declaration of shifted
}, which closes the declaration the line directive moved onto this listing
